    "caption": "Miss Piggy posed wearing the Hope Diamond. Bonnie Erickson designed her in 1974, and her pearl necklace hides the seam where her neck meets her body. In 2013, the Henson family gave her to the Smithsonian, on what would have been Jim Henson's seventy seventh birthday. The Smithsonian welcomed her with a photo shoot, where she posed wearing a necklace that held the Hope Diamond. Cade Martin shot the photos, and she also posed with Dorothy's ruby slippers. More than 20 puppets and props joined the collection that day.",
